Package: riscos-kernel-pi
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: riscos-support (>= 1.0.0001-1)
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-rolpkg
Description: Linux 6.6 kernel for RISC OS on Linux on a Raspberry Pi
 The Raspberry Pi kernel (kernel8.img), its device trees and overlays and
 the Pi's start-up firmware, on the card's FAT partition. config.txt and
 cmdline.txt are left as they are. Installing it copies them onto the FAT
 partition, keeping the old ones as *.old; a restart starts the new
 kernel.
